1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,420
It looks to be a wet one tomorrow with scattered showers throughout the day.

2
00:00:03,420 --> 00:00:06,200
Suppose I won't be hanging anything outside to dry tomorrow.

3
00:00:08,120 --> 00:00:09,400
Grandma, I'm home!

4
00:00:09,620 --> 00:00:10,800
Oh, hi. Want a snack?

5
00:00:11,200 --> 00:00:12,840
There's something I gotta check first.

6
00:00:13,740 --> 00:00:14,640
Sure, no hurry.

7
00:00:15,700 --> 00:00:17,960
Oh, come on! Why are you so slow?

8
00:00:18,260 --> 00:00:20,000
I'm not used to Ayumu's laptop.

9
00:00:20,760 --> 00:00:21,560
Here we go.

10
00:00:21,560 --> 00:00:28,560
Oh, I'm not used to...

11
00:00:28,560 --> 00:00:35,720
Whoa, holy crap!

12
00:00:36,040 --> 00:00:38,660
Yoda really is trying to gather all the Selectors together.

13
00:00:42,940 --> 00:00:45,380
It's happening really close to here, too.

14
00:00:51,560 --> 00:00:53,560
Oh, sorry.

15
00:00:53,560 --> 00:01:23,540
Thank you.

16
00:01:23,560 --> 00:01:53,540
Thank you.

17
00:01:53,560 --> 00:01:55,560
Thank you.

18
00:02:23,560 --> 00:02:24,560
Thank you.

19
00:02:24,560 --> 00:02:25,560
Thank you.

20
00:02:25,560 --> 00:02:26,560
Thank you.

21
00:02:26,560 --> 00:02:27,560
Thank you.

22
00:02:27,560 --> 00:02:28,560
Thank you.

23
00:02:28,560 --> 00:02:29,560
Thank you.

24
00:02:29,560 --> 00:02:30,560
Thank you.

25
00:02:30,560 --> 00:02:31,560
Thank you.

26
00:02:31,560 --> 00:02:32,560
Thank you.

27
00:02:32,560 --> 00:02:33,560
Thank you.

28
00:02:33,560 --> 00:02:34,560
Thank you.

29
00:02:34,560 --> 00:02:35,560
Yeah.

30
00:02:35,560 --> 00:02:36,560
Ruko?

31
00:02:36,560 --> 00:02:37,560
This is...

32
00:02:37,560 --> 00:02:54,560
They're only one building away from a Tetris, and then the whole city might just disappear

33
00:02:54,560 --> 00:02:55,560
on us.

34
00:02:55,560 --> 00:02:56,560
Ruko?

35
00:02:56,560 --> 00:03:01,560
Is something wrong?

36
00:03:01,560 --> 00:03:02,560
Uh-uh.

37
00:03:02,560 --> 00:03:04,560
Not at all.

38
00:03:04,560 --> 00:03:05,560
Ruko, listen.

39
00:03:05,560 --> 00:03:19,560
If something's bothering you, or if you've got something on your mind, say it.

40
00:03:19,560 --> 00:03:20,560
Uh...

41
00:03:20,560 --> 00:03:21,560
Yuzuki...

42
00:03:21,560 --> 00:03:24,560
Is it... true?

43
00:03:24,560 --> 00:03:26,560
Am I scary?

44
00:03:26,560 --> 00:03:29,560
Cause people say they never know what I'm thinking.

45
00:03:29,560 --> 00:03:30,560
Huh?

46
00:03:30,560 --> 00:03:32,560
No, that wasn't what I was trying to say before.

47
00:03:32,560 --> 00:03:36,560
I meant you try to figure things out all on your own and hold everything inside.

48
00:03:36,560 --> 00:03:37,560
Uh...

49
00:03:37,560 --> 00:03:40,560
You know, kinda like I do.

50
00:03:40,560 --> 00:03:42,560
I'm sorry, okay?

51
00:03:42,560 --> 00:03:44,560
Still friends, right?

52
00:03:44,560 --> 00:03:46,560
Like back when we bought these?

53
00:03:46,560 --> 00:03:49,560
Of course we are.

54
00:03:49,560 --> 00:03:52,560
You're one of the kindest people I've ever known.

55
00:03:52,560 --> 00:03:53,560
What?

56
00:03:53,560 --> 00:03:54,560
Hey, come on, knock it off.

57
00:03:54,560 --> 00:03:56,560
You're making me blush.

58
00:03:57,560 --> 00:04:00,560
Turns out you're also one of the strongest.

59
00:04:00,560 --> 00:04:01,560
Oh...

60
00:04:01,560 --> 00:04:03,560
I wish...

61
00:04:03,560 --> 00:04:05,560
I could be like that.

62
00:04:05,560 --> 00:04:09,560
Yuzuki...

63
00:04:09,560 --> 00:04:10,560
Toma...

64
00:04:10,560 --> 00:04:12,560
I'm sorry.

65
00:04:14,560 --> 00:04:17,560
I've decided to battle Iyona.

66
00:04:19,560 --> 00:04:21,560
What are you talking about?

67
00:04:21,560 --> 00:04:23,560
I thought you said you gave up battling.

68
00:04:23,560 --> 00:04:25,560
Yeah, I did.

69
00:04:26,560 --> 00:04:28,560
The thing is...

70
00:04:29,560 --> 00:04:32,560
Now, I have a wish to fight for.

71
00:04:32,560 --> 00:04:33,560
It's...

72
00:04:33,560 --> 00:04:34,560
A good one.

73
00:04:34,560 --> 00:04:36,560
It's to save you.

74
00:04:36,560 --> 00:04:37,560
You and Toma.

75
00:04:37,560 --> 00:04:40,560
Plus everyone else who became Elrigs.

76
00:04:40,560 --> 00:04:41,560
I swear.

77
00:04:41,560 --> 00:04:43,560
I'll bring you all back to normal.

78
00:04:43,560 --> 00:04:46,560
I'll get you out of this crazy game.

79
00:04:46,560 --> 00:04:49,560
I don't care what I have to sacrifice to do it.

80
00:04:49,560 --> 00:04:51,560
That's my one and only wish.

81
00:04:51,560 --> 00:04:52,560
Oh, bro.

82
00:04:52,560 --> 00:04:57,560
That's sweet, but it can't be done.

83
00:04:57,560 --> 00:04:58,560
I'm sorry.

84
00:04:58,560 --> 00:05:00,560
Why not?

85
00:05:00,560 --> 00:05:04,560
Because like me, every Elrig used to be a normal girl.

86
00:05:04,560 --> 00:05:09,560
And the Elrigs who replace winning selectors become normal girls again.

87
00:05:09,560 --> 00:05:15,560
Even though they're bound by an oath to fulfill your wish, there's a limit to what they can do.

88
00:05:19,560 --> 00:05:24,560
So you're telling me there are some wishes that can never come true, like going back in time or reshaping reality?

89
00:05:24,560 --> 00:05:26,560
That's correct.

90
00:05:26,560 --> 00:05:30,560
But it's not my place to decide which are possible and which are not.

91
00:05:30,560 --> 00:05:31,560
What?

92
00:05:31,560 --> 00:05:40,560
Most wishes can come true thanks to the efforts of the Elrig, assuming of course that she upholds her end of the oath.

93
00:05:40,560 --> 00:05:48,560
Whether it's due to personal morality, common sense, or simply a matter of self-preservation, an Elrig may become reluctant.

94
00:05:48,560 --> 00:05:54,560
But she must cast these feelings aside and prioritize the selectors' wish above her own life.

95
00:05:54,560 --> 00:06:01,560
If an Elrig refuses the wish, she will remain trapped in her card, unable to return to the outside world.

96
00:06:02,560 --> 00:06:12,560
Therefore, to guarantee both the wish and her eventual escape from her card, from the moment they meet, she must do anything and everything to reach that conclusion.

97
00:06:12,560 --> 00:06:14,560
Even deceiving her selector.

98
00:06:14,560 --> 00:06:16,560
That's what...

99
00:06:16,560 --> 00:06:19,560
Otherwise, you wouldn't agree to the ritual of acknowledgement.

100
00:06:19,560 --> 00:06:24,560
It's a catalyst, you see. A trigger for the transformation.

101
00:06:24,560 --> 00:06:28,560
Now, the oath. Do you remember it?

102
00:06:28,560 --> 00:06:31,560
Yeah. It's, uh... I accept...

103
00:06:31,560 --> 00:06:33,560
The laws of the Selector.

104
00:06:33,560 --> 00:06:36,560
I accept the laws of the Selector.

105
00:06:36,560 --> 00:06:37,560
And, um...

106
00:06:37,560 --> 00:06:40,560
And upon this sacred oath, the new Eternal Girl shall be born!

107
00:06:40,560 --> 00:06:46,560
Once an Eternal Girl, she is obligated to fulfill the wish that has been made.

108
00:06:46,560 --> 00:06:52,560
Though she may have deceived you, she has entered a contract that cannot be broken.

109
00:06:52,560 --> 00:06:57,560
For if she fails to uphold her end, the Eternal Girl will disappear.

110
00:06:57,560 --> 00:06:59,560
Remember what Hanayo said?

111
00:06:59,560 --> 00:07:03,560
About how you couldn't wish Hitoi's memories back.

112
00:07:03,560 --> 00:07:07,560
That probably means you can't just undo things with another wish.

113
00:07:07,560 --> 00:07:11,560
Yeah, but those girls, the ones who are Elric's...

114
00:07:11,560 --> 00:07:15,560
I have no idea how to get them out or if it's even possible, but...

115
00:07:15,560 --> 00:07:19,560
This Mayu girl? The one in that weird white room? She might.

116
00:07:19,560 --> 00:07:22,560
I just don't know how to get back to that place to ask her.

117
00:07:22,560 --> 00:07:24,560
Maybe I can get them out.

118
00:07:24,560 --> 00:07:25,560
Huh?

119
00:07:25,560 --> 00:07:30,560
I'm not sure why, but somewhere deep down, they feel like I might know how.

120
00:07:30,560 --> 00:07:34,560
I think I might be able to turn all the Elrics back to normal.

121
00:07:34,560 --> 00:07:35,560
Uh...

122
00:07:35,560 --> 00:07:36,560
You really think so?

123
00:07:36,560 --> 00:07:37,560
Yeah, kinda.

124
00:07:37,560 --> 00:07:40,560
But there's this feeling, something inside saying,

125
00:07:40,560 --> 00:07:42,560
Yes, I can do this thing.

126
00:07:42,560 --> 00:07:43,560
Well, maybe...

127
00:07:43,560 --> 00:07:44,560
Tama...

128
00:07:44,560 --> 00:07:46,560
Makes me wonder.

129
00:07:46,560 --> 00:07:47,560
Uh...

130
00:07:48,560 --> 00:07:50,560
No, that's crazy.

131
00:07:52,560 --> 00:07:54,560
If the Eternal Girls have so little power,

132
00:07:54,560 --> 00:07:57,560
what's the point in going through all this mess in the first place?

133
00:07:57,560 --> 00:08:00,560
We're stuck in a card and they die if they can't fulfill the wish?

134
00:08:00,560 --> 00:08:03,560
If we couldn't make the wish come true and they're us now,

135
00:08:03,560 --> 00:08:05,560
then aren't you condemning us all?

136
00:08:06,560 --> 00:08:08,560
There are exceptions.

137
00:08:09,560 --> 00:08:14,560
That is to say, some Eternal Girls are more special than others.

138
00:08:14,560 --> 00:08:18,560
You may lack the power to create this fairytale ending you so desire,

139
00:08:18,560 --> 00:08:20,560
but there is magic yet in this world.

140
00:08:20,560 --> 00:08:24,560
You expect me to buy into some fantasy mumbo-jumbo like that?

141
00:08:24,560 --> 00:08:27,560
Given what you have just been through,

142
00:08:27,560 --> 00:08:31,560
I'm surprised you would deny the very concept so flippantly.

143
00:08:31,560 --> 00:08:34,560
And now it seems the time has come.

144
00:08:42,560 --> 00:08:44,560
Morning dawns on your life as an Elric.

145
00:08:44,560 --> 00:08:46,560
You now go to meet your selector.

146
00:08:46,560 --> 00:08:48,560
No, wait! Tell me who you are!

147
00:09:01,560 --> 00:09:03,560
I'm the one who will always be here,

148
00:09:03,560 --> 00:09:07,560
in the rift that exists between the world of the cards and the world of reality.

149
00:09:07,560 --> 00:09:10,560
Good luck, and goodbye.

150
00:09:18,560 --> 00:09:21,560
You know, Tama does seem awfully different from other Elrics.

151
00:09:21,560 --> 00:09:24,560
Maybe she's one of those so-called special ones.

152
00:09:25,560 --> 00:09:27,560
So, maybe my wish can come true.

153
00:09:27,560 --> 00:09:28,560
No dice.

154
00:09:28,560 --> 00:09:29,560
What?

155
00:09:29,560 --> 00:09:31,560
Remember, if you take the oath,

156
00:09:31,560 --> 00:09:33,560
you're just going to turn into an Elric like I did.

157
00:09:34,560 --> 00:09:35,560
Right.

158
00:09:35,560 --> 00:09:36,560
But still,

159
00:09:36,560 --> 00:09:40,560
since my wish is to release all the Elrics from their cards and make them real again,

160
00:09:40,560 --> 00:09:42,560
maybe that means I won't be able to become one.

161
00:09:42,560 --> 00:09:43,560
Are you nuts?

162
00:09:44,560 --> 00:09:45,560
For all you know,

163
00:09:45,560 --> 00:09:48,560
we could get fixed while you're stuck as an Elric forever!

164
00:09:48,560 --> 00:09:50,560
Or, God forbid, something worse!

165
00:09:50,560 --> 00:09:51,560
I know, but I…

166
00:09:51,560 --> 00:09:53,560
Ruko, please! You've got to give this more thought!

167
00:09:53,560 --> 00:09:56,560
I mean, sure, if you're a card, maybe I could find you.

168
00:09:56,560 --> 00:09:59,560
And maybe we could be friends like we are now.

169
00:10:00,560 --> 00:10:01,560
But…

170
00:10:01,560 --> 00:10:03,560
People who aren't selectors,

171
00:10:03,560 --> 00:10:05,560
like your grandmother and brother,

172
00:10:05,560 --> 00:10:07,560
they'll never see you again!

173
00:10:07,560 --> 00:10:08,560
Uh…

174
00:10:12,560 --> 00:10:14,560
...

175
00:10:14,560 --> 00:10:16,560
Hitoe?

176
00:10:19,560 --> 00:10:32,560
Sorry, but I'd like my Elric back now.

177
00:10:32,560 --> 00:10:33,560
Uh…

178
00:10:33,560 --> 00:10:35,700
Hitoi, look, I, uh...

179
00:10:35,700 --> 00:10:37,680
I don't care. Just give her back, okay?

180
00:10:37,960 --> 00:10:38,520
Hitoi!

181
00:10:41,080 --> 00:10:42,660
Hold on! We need to talk!

182
00:10:43,300 --> 00:10:45,380
Yeah! Calm down! It's cool!

183
00:10:45,880 --> 00:10:46,500
I just...

184
00:10:46,500 --> 00:10:48,720
I don't want to hear it, and I have nothing to say to you.

185
00:10:49,840 --> 00:10:50,360
Hitoi!

186
00:10:54,200 --> 00:10:55,080
No way!

187
00:11:01,880 --> 00:11:02,440
Hitoi?

188
00:11:02,440 --> 00:11:06,320
I'm taking my L-Rig, and I'm going to compete in Eona's fan event.

189
00:11:07,380 --> 00:11:11,280
If you want to talk to me so badly, you can do it on the battlefield.

190
00:11:25,240 --> 00:11:28,600
If my wish comes true, I might never see Grandma again.

191
00:11:28,600 --> 00:11:36,140
What should I do?

192
00:11:38,140 --> 00:11:38,660
Grandma!

193
00:11:39,040 --> 00:11:39,920
Oh, hello.

194
00:11:40,500 --> 00:11:41,420
Yes, she's fine.

195
00:11:41,420 --> 00:11:45,040
She's even made friends.

196
00:11:45,980 --> 00:11:47,320
Hmm, she sure did.

197
00:11:50,260 --> 00:11:50,880
What's that?

198
00:11:50,880 --> 00:11:55,220
There's no point blaming yourself for this, not anymore.

199
00:11:56,220 --> 00:11:59,500
I'm tired of hearing it. This has all been settled before.

200
00:11:59,500 --> 00:12:03,380
And I won't have you pretending to be her mother, either.

201
00:12:03,380 --> 00:12:10,740
I don't hold a thing against you, but when you said you weren't meant to be a parent, I was inclined to agree, and my opinion hasn't changed.

202
00:12:11,620 --> 00:12:13,620
Remember, I love having the kids here.

203
00:12:14,000 --> 00:12:16,300
Ayumu and Ruko are both utter joys.

204
00:12:16,440 --> 00:12:17,780
They always brighten my day.

205
00:12:17,780 --> 00:12:24,260
Uh, yes. Right. Okay, I'll call you then. You take care now.

206
00:12:25,640 --> 00:12:27,980
Hi, Rue. You about ready for dinner?

207
00:12:28,840 --> 00:12:29,720
Was that Mom?

208
00:12:35,680 --> 00:12:38,080
Guess what? I finally thought of a wish.

209
00:12:38,440 --> 00:12:39,780
Oh, is that so?

210
00:12:39,780 --> 00:12:41,880
Uh-huh.

211
00:12:42,600 --> 00:12:47,580
You see, when I was little, Mom and Dad were supposed to be close, but all they did was fight.

212
00:12:48,020 --> 00:12:49,020
It made me sad.

213
00:12:50,340 --> 00:12:54,300
It made me think if you got close to someone, you'd just end up getting hurt.

214
00:12:54,640 --> 00:12:56,160
So I stayed away from people.

215
00:12:56,960 --> 00:12:59,080
Well, except for you and Ayumu, of course.

216
00:12:59,740 --> 00:13:02,200
I didn't think I needed anyone else but you guys.

217
00:13:02,200 --> 00:13:04,820
But over the last few weeks, that's changed.

218
00:13:05,500 --> 00:13:09,580
I've actually made some true friends, and they're real important to me, too.

219
00:13:09,780 --> 00:13:13,260
And it's because of them that, well...

220
00:13:13,260 --> 00:13:18,360
You were telling me the other day you hoped you could do something for your friends.

221
00:13:18,880 --> 00:13:20,740
Is this wish of yours for them?

222
00:13:22,920 --> 00:13:24,400
It's not something bad.

223
00:13:25,220 --> 00:13:27,140
No, of course not. I mean...

224
00:13:27,140 --> 00:13:28,580
So it's something good, then.

225
00:13:31,080 --> 00:13:33,340
Well, yeah. I think it is.

226
00:13:33,680 --> 00:13:34,900
It kind of has to be.

227
00:13:37,960 --> 00:13:39,680
You have a good heart, Rue.

228
00:13:39,780 --> 00:13:41,620
And you believe your wish is good.

229
00:13:42,540 --> 00:13:48,360
The very fact that you wished it for your friends instead of for yourself proves to me you're probably on the right track.

230
00:13:48,760 --> 00:13:50,500
So you do what you need to, dear.

231
00:13:50,740 --> 00:13:52,260
And I'm sure it will come true.

232
00:13:52,920 --> 00:13:55,920
Your friends are very lucky to have you, and so am I.

233
00:13:56,560 --> 00:13:56,960
Grandma!

234
00:13:58,000 --> 00:13:59,300
Oh, it's all right.

235
00:13:59,360 --> 00:14:00,640
There's no reason to cry.

236
00:14:00,840 --> 00:14:01,360
Who?

237
00:14:10,440 --> 00:14:10,960
Rue?

238
00:14:11,280 --> 00:14:11,600
Huh?

239
00:14:11,600 --> 00:14:14,660
So you're gonna battle?

240
00:14:15,640 --> 00:14:16,080
Mm-hmm.

241
00:14:16,720 --> 00:14:19,200
We're gonna take on that mean girl, Leona, again.

242
00:14:19,500 --> 00:14:20,460
I bet you can't wait.

243
00:14:20,500 --> 00:14:21,780
No, I don't want to!

244
00:14:22,060 --> 00:14:22,240
Huh?

245
00:14:22,920 --> 00:14:24,700
Your grandma doesn't know what could happen.

246
00:14:25,300 --> 00:14:27,240
If she did, she wouldn't have said all that.

247
00:14:27,440 --> 00:14:29,160
She wouldn't let you risk your life.

248
00:14:29,240 --> 00:14:31,600
I don't care if I'm stuck in this dump cart forever.

249
00:14:31,760 --> 00:14:33,060
It's better than being alone.

250
00:14:33,300 --> 00:14:35,520
You may never see me or your grandma again.

251
00:14:35,700 --> 00:14:37,280
So please don't do this, Rue.

252
00:14:37,300 --> 00:14:38,760
I don't want to lose you.

253
00:14:38,760 --> 00:14:43,660
But Tama, I'm sure my plan is gonna work.

254
00:14:43,780 --> 00:14:45,540
But Yuzuki said it might not.

255
00:14:45,820 --> 00:14:46,820
Then what'll happen?

256
00:14:48,680 --> 00:14:50,840
I'm sorry, but I've gotta do this.

257
00:14:51,300 --> 00:14:54,500
I won't become an L-Rig and I won't let you stay one.

258
00:14:54,760 --> 00:14:55,560
I promise.

259
00:14:56,120 --> 00:14:57,580
We'll never be apart.

260
00:14:59,680 --> 00:15:02,500
Really, you and I will do everything together.

261
00:15:02,500 --> 00:15:08,880
Have yummy breakfasts with grandma.

262
00:15:10,960 --> 00:15:12,680
Runs or not late to school.

263
00:15:13,860 --> 00:15:15,800
Hang out with Yuzuki and Hitoi.

264
00:15:16,220 --> 00:15:17,900
We'll all be best friends.

265
00:15:19,000 --> 00:15:20,980
It's closed now, but during the summer.

266
00:15:21,500 --> 00:15:23,100
We'll go to the candy shop on the corner.

267
00:15:23,560 --> 00:15:25,660
They've got this ice cream you wouldn't believe.

268
00:15:25,980 --> 00:15:27,620
We'll try a new flavor every day.

269
00:15:28,620 --> 00:15:30,420
Trust me, you'll love it.

270
00:15:32,500 --> 00:15:39,220
So, sound good?

271
00:15:39,560 --> 00:15:40,380
It does.

272
00:15:41,240 --> 00:15:42,060
But no.

273
00:15:43,280 --> 00:15:44,740
Don't do it.

274
00:15:46,280 --> 00:15:47,980
I'm sorry, Tama.

275
00:15:48,480 --> 00:15:49,580
I am.

276
00:15:51,100 --> 00:15:54,440
But I have to finish this.

277
00:15:55,140 --> 00:15:56,420
Be careful now.

278
00:15:56,540 --> 00:15:57,320
Okay, Rue?

279
00:15:57,600 --> 00:15:58,080
Okay.

280
00:15:58,080 --> 00:16:00,420
Think you'll be home in time for dinner?

281
00:16:01,540 --> 00:16:02,580
Good question.

282
00:16:04,220 --> 00:16:05,080
I'll try.

283
00:16:05,980 --> 00:16:08,380
And do you think we could have potatoes au gratin?

284
00:16:08,580 --> 00:16:10,320
With lots of bacon the way you like?

285
00:16:10,400 --> 00:16:11,180
Oh, please.

286
00:16:11,960 --> 00:16:12,820
Love you, Grandma.

287
00:16:12,820 --> 00:16:17,020
All right.

288
00:16:21,340 --> 00:16:22,320
Here goes.

289
00:16:22,320 --> 00:16:31,180
Oh, wow.

290
00:16:31,780 --> 00:16:32,720
These girls.

291
00:16:33,460 --> 00:16:36,120
All of them are selectors here to fight for their wishes.

292
00:16:36,120 --> 00:16:49,620
Ladies, welcome to the fan event.

293
00:16:50,500 --> 00:16:54,380
Rather, welcome to the selectors-only WeCross party.

294
00:16:55,340 --> 00:16:59,240
This building is owned by my father, and the work crews are off today.

295
00:16:59,460 --> 00:17:02,060
So we don't have to worry about being disturbed.

296
00:17:02,060 --> 00:17:06,140
We've all been battling to make our wishes come true.

297
00:17:06,880 --> 00:17:10,520
And yet, we don't know how many wins we need to make that happen.

298
00:17:11,380 --> 00:17:12,320
Frustrating, isn't it?

299
00:17:13,200 --> 00:17:14,320
I started to wonder.

300
00:17:14,780 --> 00:17:17,120
What if there was something we could do to change that?

301
00:17:17,680 --> 00:17:18,700
Hence this party.

302
00:17:19,220 --> 00:17:21,460
With so many selectors gathered to do battle.

303
00:17:22,120 --> 00:17:25,000
Some are bound to win enough to meet these elusive conditions.

304
00:17:25,000 --> 00:17:30,080
As a result, a large number of eternal girls will be born right here today.

305
00:17:30,320 --> 00:17:31,300
These selectors.

306
00:17:31,640 --> 00:17:32,640
They have no clue.

307
00:17:33,560 --> 00:17:37,700
Now, obviously, for each of you who wins, there will be another who loses.

308
00:17:38,460 --> 00:17:43,340
Speaking personally, I have no desire to fight anyone but the strongest selectors available.

309
00:17:46,240 --> 00:17:48,740
Therefore, I have assigned you all to tournament brackets.

310
00:17:49,340 --> 00:17:51,660
If you win a battle, you progress to the next round.

311
00:17:52,000 --> 00:17:53,160
If you lose, you're out.

312
00:17:53,160 --> 00:17:56,200
This will at least prevent multiple losses.

313
00:17:57,000 --> 00:17:59,240
And the selector who makes it all the way to the top?

314
00:17:59,800 --> 00:18:01,820
Well, you'll be facing me, of course.

315
00:18:10,820 --> 00:18:12,900
Twelfth floor, room four?

316
00:18:23,160 --> 00:18:24,200
Is everyone ready?

317
00:18:25,040 --> 00:18:25,940
I hope so.

318
00:18:27,000 --> 00:18:28,880
Because the battle begins now.

319
00:18:29,620 --> 00:18:30,220
Open!

320
00:18:30,220 --> 00:18:41,620
Tama Grove, gothic foundry.

321
00:18:44,620 --> 00:18:46,060
I know it hurts.

322
00:18:46,520 --> 00:18:49,920
But when I'm finished, none of you will ever have to go through this again.

323
00:18:50,480 --> 00:18:51,580
Summon Mitsuruki.

324
00:18:52,060 --> 00:18:53,520
This is the final blow, Tama.

325
00:18:55,560 --> 00:18:55,960
Tama?

326
00:18:55,960 --> 00:18:56,640
Tama!

327
00:19:05,140 --> 00:19:05,660
Tama!

328
00:19:07,420 --> 00:19:09,320
Please, I need you to agree to this.

329
00:19:10,020 --> 00:19:11,740
Otherwise, my wish won't come true.

330
00:19:13,060 --> 00:19:14,420
I'm sorry, Tama.

331
00:19:14,420 --> 00:19:16,660
But we have to do it my way.

332
00:19:19,780 --> 00:19:21,420
We have to keep battling.

333
00:19:29,880 --> 00:19:31,660
I should have seen this coming.

334
00:19:32,960 --> 00:19:33,780
Guess so.

335
00:19:34,260 --> 00:19:35,700
You ready to talk to me now?

336
00:19:35,700 --> 00:19:37,680
Like I said, on the battlefield.

337
00:19:43,720 --> 00:19:44,240
Open!

338
00:19:51,880 --> 00:19:54,060
No new eternal girls have been born yet.

339
00:19:54,280 --> 00:19:55,260
Not that I sense.

340
00:19:55,660 --> 00:19:56,320
Oh, well.

341
00:19:56,620 --> 00:19:57,560
On the other hand,

342
00:19:57,640 --> 00:20:00,940
it looks like some selectors are losing their third and final battles.

343
00:20:00,940 --> 00:20:10,640
I will find my way there.

344
00:20:11,300 --> 00:20:12,360
To that white room.

345
00:20:13,100 --> 00:20:14,200
Where she's waiting.

346
00:20:15,780 --> 00:20:17,640
Mount Sevieryia and attack!

347
00:20:20,860 --> 00:20:21,540
Yuzuki!

348
00:20:21,800 --> 00:20:22,380
Grow now!

349
00:20:23,120 --> 00:20:25,160
And banish Mikigami!

350
00:20:25,160 --> 00:20:30,520
Dang it.

351
00:20:31,000 --> 00:20:32,520
She's so much better than before.

352
00:20:33,260 --> 00:20:34,460
Splitting conviction.

353
00:20:35,740 --> 00:20:36,340
Tama!

354
00:20:36,680 --> 00:20:37,120
Sorry!

355
00:20:41,760 --> 00:20:42,880
Yuzuki, attack!

356
00:20:43,220 --> 00:20:44,120
Banish Square!

357
00:20:44,820 --> 00:20:45,280
Hit away.

358
00:20:46,480 --> 00:20:47,460
It's wrong.

359
00:20:48,180 --> 00:20:49,500
It's all wrong.

360
00:20:49,800 --> 00:20:51,000
What do you mean, wrong?

361
00:20:51,500 --> 00:20:53,620
It's not supposed to be like this.

362
00:20:53,620 --> 00:20:56,640
Why can't you remember how it was when we played before?

363
00:20:57,900 --> 00:20:58,420
Ruko.

364
00:20:58,960 --> 00:21:00,400
We used to play for fun.

365
00:21:00,900 --> 00:21:01,680
Not to win.

366
00:21:02,120 --> 00:21:02,900
No Elrigs.

367
00:21:02,960 --> 00:21:03,520
No battles.

368
00:21:03,660 --> 00:21:04,160
No wishes.

369
00:21:05,400 --> 00:21:06,320
Back then,

370
00:21:06,540 --> 00:21:08,380
I thought that wasn't enough.

371
00:21:08,520 --> 00:21:09,980
I wanted serious battles.

372
00:21:10,140 --> 00:21:10,860
Serious victories.

373
00:21:11,260 --> 00:21:13,380
Instead of just appreciating what I had.

374
00:21:13,920 --> 00:21:14,560
Me too.

375
00:21:14,920 --> 00:21:15,820
Now it's gone.

376
00:21:16,380 --> 00:21:19,500
We can never just enjoy playing games again as friends.

377
00:21:20,940 --> 00:21:22,220
And I hate it.

378
00:21:22,220 --> 00:21:26,900
I knew it.

379
00:21:27,400 --> 00:21:28,540
Now she's sad too.

380
00:21:29,500 --> 00:21:31,520
That means she must remember.

381
00:21:32,220 --> 00:21:33,800
She still has memories of us.

382
00:21:34,180 --> 00:21:35,100
You think?

383
00:21:35,640 --> 00:21:36,480
Hitoi, listen.

384
00:21:37,040 --> 00:21:39,140
Like Ruko said, we all used to be friends.

385
00:21:39,760 --> 00:21:40,060
What?

386
00:21:41,000 --> 00:21:42,000
No, stop!

387
00:21:42,000 --> 00:21:42,800
Did that hurt?

388
00:21:42,800 --> 00:21:43,940
I'm sorry.

389
00:21:44,760 --> 00:21:46,240
But I need you to remember.

390
00:21:47,980 --> 00:21:49,260
Knock it off, Yuzuki!

391
00:21:49,360 --> 00:21:50,240
You're hurting her!

392
00:21:50,240 --> 00:21:52,560
I know, but do you want her to stay like this?

393
00:21:53,600 --> 00:21:56,160
Her life being controlled by these stupid battles?

394
00:21:56,920 --> 00:21:57,640
I don't.

395
00:21:58,180 --> 00:22:00,140
I want to be best friends like we were!

396
00:22:00,760 --> 00:22:01,460
Me too!

397
00:22:01,540 --> 00:22:03,000
I don't want to battle like this!

398
00:22:03,420 --> 00:22:05,780
I want to do it as friends like we used to!

399
00:22:06,200 --> 00:22:07,320
It was so much fun!

400
00:22:07,420 --> 00:22:08,220
Please remember!

401
00:22:08,340 --> 00:22:09,480
No, please stop it!

402
00:22:09,580 --> 00:22:10,500
This is killing me!

403
00:22:10,720 --> 00:22:11,900
Hitoi, remember!

404
00:22:12,700 --> 00:22:14,760
Your wish to make friends already came true!

405
00:22:15,300 --> 00:22:17,000
You can quit all of this!

406
00:22:17,300 --> 00:22:18,360
You still have us!

407
00:22:18,520 --> 00:22:19,040
Stop it!

408
00:22:19,400 --> 00:22:20,020
Stop it!

409
00:22:20,220 --> 00:22:20,880
Stop it!

410
00:22:20,960 --> 00:22:22,220
You can do this, Hitoi!

411
00:22:22,220 --> 00:22:23,720
Just remember how it used to be!

412
00:22:24,040 --> 00:22:25,540
Would you please just shut up?

413
00:22:25,540 --> 00:22:27,720
I don't want to hear any more of this!

414
00:22:28,200 --> 00:22:30,880
I just want to make my wish come true, that's all!

415
00:22:31,220 --> 00:22:32,060
Aren't you listening?

416
00:22:32,200 --> 00:22:33,660
I told you, it already did!

417
00:22:33,940 --> 00:22:34,360
So...

418
00:22:34,360 --> 00:22:35,140
Stop it!

419
00:22:36,480 --> 00:22:37,480
No, okay!

420
00:22:37,660 --> 00:22:39,020
This wasn't part of the deal!

421
00:22:39,580 --> 00:22:42,580
You promised we would battle and you'd grant me a wish!

422
00:22:46,340 --> 00:22:47,300
I...

423
00:22:47,300 --> 00:22:49,520
Where's Crunchy?

424
00:22:50,220 --> 00:22:51,360
She still has it!

425
00:22:54,160 --> 00:22:55,360
Now then...

426
00:22:55,540 --> 00:22:56,960
Ready to say goodbye!

427
00:22:59,880 --> 00:23:01,740
I've waited long enough already!

428
00:23:02,580 --> 00:23:05,880
Soon I will face my final battle as Yona Uruzoe!

429
00:23:06,260 --> 00:23:07,580
Oh, one final note!

430
00:23:07,960 --> 00:23:11,100
What's been a blast giving beatdowns to other Selectors with you!

431
00:23:11,980 --> 00:23:14,520
I'm not gonna miss you one bit, you rotten bitch!

432
00:23:19,020 --> 00:23:21,660
Still, I'll be beside you to the very end!

433
00:23:22,660 --> 00:23:23,100
Selector!

434
00:23:23,100 --> 00:23:35,260
Next time, that choice!

435
00:23:35,260 --> 00:23:37,660
Next time, that choice!

436
00:23:37,660 --> 00:23:39,800
Next time, that choice.

